{
    "background_story": "Trevor was a renowned botanist with a passion for the Erythroxylaceae family, commonly known as the coca family. Growing up in the Amazon rainforest, he was fascinated by the unique properties of these plants. Trevor spent years studying the Erythroxylum coca, uncovering its secrets and learning about its traditional uses by indigenous communities. His research led to groundbreaking discoveries about the plant's medicinal properties, and he became a leading expert in the field. Trevor's work took him to remote corners of the world, from the Andes to the Congo Basin, where he collaborated with local communities to preserve and study the Erythroxylaceae family. His dedication to the field earned him the nickname 'The Coca Whisperer' among his peers.",
